# CVE-2019-5477: the rexical-generated CSS tokenizer opened its input file
# through Ruby's receiverless `open`. `Kernel#open` is mixed into Object, so
# `open path, "r"` is `Kernel.open path, "r"`, and Ruby documents that method as
# running the path as a subprocess command line whenever its first character is
# `|`. `Tokenizer#load_file` takes the path straight from its caller and
# `scan_file` forwards to it, so an application that tokenises a caller-named
# stylesheet runs `id` for a path spelled `|id` (CWE-78). The fixed revision regenerates the
# lexer with rexical 1.0.7, which emits `File.open` -- the spelling that has no
# pipe behaviour.
#
# The weakness class is existing vocabulary: code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution,
# its review twin and VYQL-INJ-042. The receiverless spelling is bound exactly
# (callee.path == "open"), because `~=` is segment-aware in both directions and
# would otherwise pull in the patched `File.open` as well.
#
# The path arrives as a library method parameter rather than from a labelled
# source, so this is the review direction: the flag names the call for a caller
# audit, and the taint rule stays silent until a source reaches it.

test "rank1464: a lexer input path opened through bare open can run a piped path"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/nokogiri/css/tokenizer.rb
  code
  ```
  module Nokogiri
  module CSS
  class Tokenizer
    require 'strscan'

    attr_reader :filename

    def scan_setup(str)
      @ss = StringScanner.new(str)
      @lineno = 1
      @state = nil
    end

    def load_file( filename )
      @filename = filename
      open(filename, "r") do |f|
        scan_setup(f.read)
      end
    end

    def scan_file( filename )
      load_file(filename)
      do_parse
    end
  end
  end
  end
  ```

test "rank1464: the regenerated lexer opens the same path through File.open"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/nokogiri/css/tokenizer.rb
  code
  ```
  module Nokogiri
  module CSS
  class Tokenizer
    require 'strscan'

    attr_reader :filename

    def scan_setup(str)
      @ss = StringScanner.new(str)
      @lineno = 1
      @state = nil
    end

    def load_file( filename )
      @filename = filename
      File.open(filename, "r") do |f|
        scan_setup(f.read)
      end
    end

    def scan_file( filename )
      load_file(filename)
      do_parse
    end
  end
  end
  end
  ```
